<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johannes van den Bosch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1780">1780</a>–<a href="/years/1844">1844</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Van den Bosch</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johannes van den Bosch was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Governor-General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>. In 1830 he introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultivation-system">Cultivation System</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, which forced peasants to devote part of their land or labour to export crops for the colonial government. The system generated large profits for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> but caused great hardship in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>'s colony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johannes-van-den-bosch.jpg" alt="Johannes van den Bosch" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raden Saleh · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raden_Sarief_Bastaman_Saleh_-_Johannes_Graaf_van_den_Bosch.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The colony’s economy was shaped by the Cultivation System (cultuurstelsel) introduced by Governor-General <b>Johannes van den Bosch</b> in 1830.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dutch-east-indies">Dutch East Indies · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>In Java, the Cultivation System introduced by Governor-General <b>Johannes van den Bosch</b> in 1830 required villages to devote a portion of their land, nominally one-fifth, or their labour to export crops such as coffee, sugar and indigo for the colonial state, generating remittances that by the 1850s and…</blockquote><a href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the cultivation system introduced in Java in 1830 by <b>Johannes van den Bosch</b>, villagers had to grow export crops such as coffee, sugar and indigo for the government, and the profits supplied a large share of Dutch state revenue until the system was dismantled after 1870.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Herwijnen, in what is now <a href="/countries/netherlands">the Netherlands</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/netherlands">the Netherlands</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.83,5.13&amp;year=1821" aria-label="Herwijnen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4666 372 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Johannes van den Bosch"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5116 642h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5116 642h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.83,5.13&amp;year=1821">What was here in 1821? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
